  "strategy": "This solution uses a Reflection-Share hybrid optimization approach with full linear convolution and minimal peak penalty. It starts from multiple length configurations (400, 800, 1000, 10000) and applies both interior point and exterior point search strategies to find sequences with better objective values.\n\nThe algorithm consists of five main phases:\n1. Initial reflection search expands the solution space by negativing projections\n2. Interior LP polishing uses proportional increase directions\n3. Exterior search continues reflection at increasing distances\n4. Heuristic deltas apply exponential shifts\n5. Final refinement uses ternary search for minimal peak\n\nKey improvements over previous methods include:\n- Dynamic length selection with BPROP to balance optimization quality and computational cost\n- Three reflection strategies (delta, gamma, expansion) to explore high peak-to-sum regions\n- A probabilistic recombination mechanism inspired by genetic algorithms\n- Convergence checks via exact evalutations rather than heuristic steps\n\nThe approach builds upon the previous program's objective function and optimization framework but implements more robust search strategies. Each candidate is explicitly checked by the evaluator, and the best sequence is preserved throughout.\n\nParameters are carefully adapted: reflection shifts are 1.5, interior steps 100, exterior combines 4 points with adaptive scale. These ensure meaningful progression without excessive computations.\n\nThe solution strictly adheres to the non-negative coefficient rule and respects coefficient bounds, never letting normalization affect the search process.\n\nThis thorough check and recombination mechanism prevent stagnation in local minima and produce more resilient optimization outcomes.",
